    <!-- Mirrors the README "Privacy" section; keep the two in sync. -->
    <string name="privacy_html"><![CDATA[
<p>HomeWx has no account, no ads and no advertising ID, does not ask for location permission, and does not sell or share data for marketing.</p>
<p><b>1. Home ZIP code</b> (optional)<br/>Stored on this tablet. Sent once to api.zippopotam.us to find its center point, which is then sent to the weather, rain and river services (Open-Meteo, WxData / weather.com, ACIS, Iowa Mesonet, USGS) to get data for your area, including river gauges and rain totals, and marks home on the radar map. The device\'s own GPS position is never read.</p>
<p><b>2. Wyze email and password</b> (optional)<br/>Stored on this tablet only, encrypted. Entered into the Wyze sign-in page to open your cameras. Not sent anywhere else.</p>
<p><b>3. Govee API key</b> (optional)<br/>Stored on this tablet only, encrypted. Sent to Govee\'s API to read your sensors. Not sent anywhere else.</p>
<p><b>4. WxData API key</b> (optional, wxdata build only)<br/>Stored on this tablet only, encrypted. Sent to api.weather.com to get weather. Not sent anywhere else.</p>
<p><b>5. Sensor, weather, river and rain history</b><br/>Stored on this tablet only. Export writes it to a file you choose; credentials are never included.</p>
<p><b>6. Usage analytics</b> (Firebase Analytics, on by default)<br/>Anonymous usage counts and device info (model, OS and app version, country), tied to a random ID. Stored in Google Cloud and managed by Google.</p>
<p><b>7. Crash and error reports</b> (Firebase Crashlytics, on by default)<br/>Crash stack traces and handled errors with device info. An error message can include a Govee device name or a server\'s error text. Stored in Google Cloud and managed by Google.</p>
<p>Google deletes crash reports after 90 days and analytics data after 2 months (Firebase defaults).</p>
<p><b>8. Error log</b> (Settings &gt; Errors)<br/>Kept on this tablet only, in memory: the last 5 errors, cleared when the app restarts or you tap Clear. Not sent anywhere unless you tap Share, which lets you pick the app and the recipient. Each entry has the time, which feature failed, the error message and technical details. These can include a Govee device name, a news feed name or a server\'s error text, but never credentials.</p>
<p><b>9. News, maps and web pages</b><br/>RSS feeds, articles, map tiles, the stock widget and the drought map are loaded from their sites, which see your IP address and may set cookies.</p>
<p><b>10. Android backup</b><br/>If backup is on for this tablet, Android may back up app settings (including the ZIP code) to your Google account. Saved credentials can\'t be read after a restore.</p>
<p><b>Opting out:</b> clear items 1 to 4 here in Settings, and item 8 with Clear in Errors. Turn off <i>Send anonymous usage stats and crash reports</i> above to stop Firebase reporting; this also discards unsent crash reports and resets the analytics ID. Data already sent can\'t be deleted from the app and expires as above. Uninstalling the app deletes everything it stored on this tablet.</p>
<p><b>Permissions</b><br/>
<b>Internet, network state:</b> fetch weather, maps, news and river data, and detect when the network is down.<br/>
<b>Foreground service and notifications:</b> keep updates running while the dashboard is on, shown by an ongoing notification. Updates slow down when the room is dark.<br/>
<b>Wake lock, Play install referrer:</b> added by Firebase Analytics, to send reports and record how the app was installed.<br/>
<b>Run at startup:</b> reopens the dashboard after the tablet restarts.<br/>
No location, camera, microphone, contacts, photos or storage permission is used. A background-image folder is read only if you pick one in Settings.</p>
<p>Full privacy policy: <a href="https://landenlabs.github.io/all-HomeWx/privacy-policy.html">https://landenlabs.github.io/all-HomeWx/privacy-policy.html</a></p>
]]></string>

